<p style="text-align:justify;">
<a href="#world" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">Game world</b></a><br>
<a href="#diff" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">Are there any differences between worlds?</b></a><br>
<a href="#resource" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">What resources are there in the game?</b></a><br>
<a href="#war" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">War system of Destiny Sphere</b></a><br>
<a href="#gate" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">What are Central Gates and newbie defense?</b></a><br>
<a href="#rating" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">What is rating?</b></a><br>
<a href="#firststep" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">First steps in the game</b></a><br>
<a href="#questions" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">I have more questions!</b></a><br><br>


<a name="world" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">Game world</b></a><br>
There are three game races: Voraners, Liensu and Psolao. <br>
Voraners is a tech-race (very strong in attack and have a lot of caderium), Liensu are genetics (a lot of units and food) and Psolao are mages (armies of mages and artifacts). 
</p>
<p style="text-align:justify;">
Each player automatically gets his own comb right after he registers in the game. Home comb is the fist available territory for the new player. For each field type there are buildings to be built there. Some building can be built not only on one field type, some – only on one.
</p>
<p style="text-align:justify;">
On the next step, after activation of the central gates, each player gets also central and neutral combs. Central comb consists of ground and rocks, neutral – of desert.
</p>
<p style="text-align:justify;">
Each six combs are the complex and all the complexes of one race are the ring. Each game world consists of four rings:
<p>
<span style="color:lightgreen">Vorania</span> – place where voraners live.<br>
<span style="color:lightgreen">Liensord</span> – place where liensu live.<br>
<span style="color:lightgreen">Psoleon</span> – place where psolao live.<br>
<span style="color:lightgreen">Melsion</span> – colonization ring. All three races can live there.<br>
</p>

<p style="text-align:justify;">
<a name="diff" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">Are there any differences between worlds?</b></a><br>
After registration you will have to choose the world in which you will play. Each world has its own unique points. The speed of the world (the speed of buildings construction and amount of buildings for simultaneous building, speed of flights and so on), it’s type (about different world types you can read here), technical settings – all that differs one world from another. We advise you to start the game with choosing the type of the game and creating your comb in one of newbie worlds. After you feel free in the game you can move to another world which you prefer most.
</p>
<p style="text-align:justify;">
In Destiny Sphere there are two types of the worlds: Each vs Each or Race vs Race. In the world of first type you can fight with anyone you want no matter what race he is, in the second world type you can fight only with players of other races and that provides you additional defense (your neighbor won’t attack you at least).
</p>
<p style="text-align:justify;">
From the very beginning of Destiny Sphere in each type of the world there are different war tactics and ways to develop. It’s up to you to choose!
</p>
<p style="text-align:justify;">
<a name="resource" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">What resources are there in the game?</b></a><br>
There are five resources that can be produced in Destiny Sphere:<br><br>

<span style="color:lightgreen">Caderium</span><br>
<span style="color:lightgreen">Nano-Crystals</span><br>
<span style="color:lightgreen">Food</span><br>
<span style="color:lightgreen">Energy</span><br>
<span style="color:lightgreen">Prodium</span><br>

</p>
<p style="text-align:justify;">
In every strategy game the resources are very important. They give the opportunity to build and to create war units, train archeologists and scientists, support your army. Resources are used in trade and are expensive prize in battle’s victory. The first production of resources you can organize by building producing buildings. Then, learning higher science levels, you can make buildings of higher level, producing more resources. Workers can be trained to be scientists and archeologists and also from them you will make armies.</p>
<p style="text-align:justify;">
<a name="war" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">War system of Destiny Sphere</b></a><br>
Battles are one of the most important parts of “Destiny Sphere. In some time you will have your own war tactic and will compose armies for attack and defense in a right way. For battles you need war units that are divided on 4 classes depending on factory which produces it and its force. You can look through the different war factories here.
</p>
<p style="text-align:justify;">
Each unit has 4 parameters: attack, defense, damage and armor. The scheme of the battle is quite simple: the player makes an army of some units, puts in his opponent’s coordinates and sends his army in attack. For some time the army moves to opponent’s comb, then the battle which is automatic starts. After that the army returns no matter if it won or lost the battle. The unique point of the battle is that you can take part in the battle on-line changing its result.
</p>
<p style="text-align:justify;">
During 6 year history of “Destiny Sphere” there were found a lot of techniques of attack and defense. There are some classic schemes but sometimes these schemes can be changes in aim of confusing the opponent. Make experiments and maybe you will make the new ideal scheme in enemy’s armies destroying.  
</p>
<p style="text-align:justify;">
<a name="gate" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">What are Central Gates and newbie defense?</b></a><br>
At the beginning of the game you are not exposed to danger from other players. You can develop in peace to some level if you won’t repair Central Gates too fast. From the one side it makes the game less dynamical as nor you can attack not you can be attacked. 
But on the other side it gives you ability to look through the game, build some needed buildings, research some sciences. But for the further development you will need to open the gates. 

</p>
<p style="text-align:justify;">
And even if you do it you will be under newbie defense for the first time, it’ll give you the time to see your new abilities and build defense buildings if you will need it. Newbie defense will protect you only for some time but it will be taken off earlier if you enter some alliance or attack someone yourself. 
</p>

<p style="text-align:justify;">
<a name="rating" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">What is rating?</b></a><br>
You develop, collect army, search for the artifacts, research sciences, fight and win. So your self-assertion grows as your ratings. Ratings show how developed you are and how dangerous you are as well. 
<br>
There are two ratings:<br>
Common rating. It shows the level of your common progress and depends on your science research levels, 
building levels and so on. War rating. It grows for the opponent’s armies’ destruction
</p>

<p style="text-align:justify;">
<a name="firststep" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">First steps in the game</b></a><br>

You have registered and entered the game. The first thing you see is your game territory, your home. You can see three buildings there:
<br><br>

<span style="color:lightgreen">Storage</span> – there you can see your economics<br>
<span style="color:lightgreen">Fragments of central gates</span> –  your future enter to the game world<br>
<span style="color:lightgreen">Construction Factory</span> – the building which gives you resources and ability to construct other buildings.<br>
</p>
<p style="text-align:justify;">
At first you have some few amount of resources, use it for further development of your comb choosing this or that buildings to construct. About what to build and how to do it you can read here. Be careful and watch out you resources balance not to become negative. Though if it happens it’s not a big trouble – you can temporally deactivate some buildings and activate it again when needed.
</p>

<p style="text-align:justify;">
<a name="questions" style="text-decoration:none"><b style="color:yellow">I have more questions!</b></a><br>
If you have more questions you can search for the answers in our FAQ or ask for help on special newbie forum.
</p>
